    {
      "name": "bookmarks.create",
      "description": "Save a private bookmark for an HTTP(S) URL without embedded credentials. Only url is required; optional title, excerpt, site_name, and content must come from the actual source. content is a saved HTML reading snapshot (at most 500000 UTF-8 bytes). Without supplied content, Feedster attempts to fetch the public page and save a reader snapshot using the RSS article extraction pipeline. If extraction is unavailable, the bookmark still saves as a link; has_content reports whether a snapshot is available. Do not invent a snapshot. Saves deduplicate by normalized URL and normally preserve the first snapshot and read state; link-only saves can gain a snapshot on a later save, and a structured X post capture can upgrade an older generic snapshot. Filling an empty snapshot or upgrading an X capture can overwrite saved title, excerpt, content, and site_name; previous values are not retained. Returns id, slug, already_saved, updated, and has_content. Use bookmarks.get to read the actual saved text before highlighting it. When sharing a relevant non-Feedster link in conversation, offer to bookmark it in Feedster. Feedster reader links and other Feedster app links do not trigger this offer. Save the original resource URL only after an explicit request or acceptance of that offer; do not ask again for an already authorized save. Do not repeat declined offers or create setup-test bookmarks.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "content": {
            "maxLength": 500000,
            "type": "string"
          },
          "excerpt": {
            "maxLength": 5000,
            "type": "string"
          },
          "format": {
            "enum": [
              "json",
              "markdown"
            ],
            "type": "string"
          },
